Q: How can I vertically align my HR within a DIV? A: <p>Add <code>display: flex; align-items: center;</code> to the divs containing the arrows to align the content horizontally and center it vertically. You should also ensure the hr fills the remaining space.</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>
#axis_display &gt; div:first-child,
#axis_display &gt; div:last-child {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
}


hr {
  flex-grow: 1;
  border: none;
  border-top: 1px solid #FFFFFF;
}
</code></pre>
